{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210734,"nonce":"nxuVJzm2dX2W409lOnYzwh6CCtw=","title":"AOT trace_object SIGSEGV: plugin foreign methods held Rust-local Values across nursery GC","message":"Fixed in commit 9aeabba. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n\nRandom SIGSEGV during AOT runs of procedural-world:\n- Crash in `trace_object` during `Gc::collect_minor` during `finish_alloc`\n- `far` = `0xfffc0005d4026809` (NaN-boxed-bits + 1 byte) — GC dereferencing an unmasked Value as `*mut ObjHeader`\n- Plugin entry points: `wlift_gpu_surface_acquire` (alloc_map) and `wlift_window_drain_events` (alloc_list)\n\n\nForeign methods doing multi-allocation work held stale `Value`\nRust-locals across nursery GCs. After forwarding, the locals\ndecoded to the pre-promotion pointer; the next `map_set` /\n`list_add` wrote through the zombie cell — smearing NaN-tagged\nValue bits into the next allocation's `ObjHeader.class` slot.\nThe NEXT GC's `trace_object` then dereferenced that field as a\nclass pointer and faulted.\n\nThe pattern was DOCUMENTED in `wlift_gpu::buffer_read_bytes`\n(re-reads `slot(0)` each iteration) but never generalised. The\nworst offenders had per-iteration handles (`map`, `key_type`,\n\"code\"/\"button\" strings) that bypassed the discipline.\n\n\n`infer_osr_value_types` in `src/codegen/cranelift_backend.rs`\ninitialises every value's type to `MirType::Void` and only\nupdates entries based on `block.params` + instruction defs.\nEntry-block BlockParam instructions (function args including\n`this`) never get their type set to `MirType::Value`, so the\n`is_wren_value` gate at the entry-block param-marking site\nreturns false and Cranelift never adds them to the stack map.\nReceiver register can stale across a callee's GC.\n\n\n1. **New rooting primitives in `wlift_abi`**:\n   - `wlift_plugin_jit_roots_snapshot(vm) -\u003e u32`\n   - `wlift_plugin_push_root(vm, value) -\u003e u32`\n   - `wlift_plugin_jit_root_at(vm, idx) -\u003e u64`\n   - `wlift_plugin_jit_roots_restore(vm, depth)`\n\n   Implemented as thin wrappers over existing `runtime_fns::push_jit_root`\n   / `jit_root_at` / `jit_roots_snapshot_len` / `jit_roots_restore_len`.\n   Additive to the ABI — old plugins keep loading.\n\n2. **`wlift_window::drain_events`**: every per-iteration handle\n   wraps `push_root` / `reload_root`; `roots_snapshot` at function\n   entry; `roots_restore` between iterations and on exit.\n\n3. **`wlift_gpu::surface_acquire`**: re-reads the map via `slot(vm, 0)`\n   (set_return roots it there) for each `map_set` call.\n\n4. **`cranelift_backend.rs:2873`**: drop the `is_wren_value` gate\n   for entry-block BlockParam args — they're all i64 Wren Value\n   bits by ABI construction; mark unconditionally.\n\n\nIf a foreign method does N allocations AND carries any Value\nbetween them, **every receiver carried across an allocator call\nmust be GC-rooted**. Choices:\n\n- Single root: use `set_return(vm, value)` + `slot(vm, 0)` for\n  re-read (the simplest case, e.g. surface_acquire).\n- Multi-root: `roots_snapshot` / `push_root` / `reload_root` /\n  `roots_restore` from `wlift_abi`.\n\nAudit candidate list (per workflow w699ptuhk):\n- `wlift_sqlite` — multi-row result builds\n- `wlift_audio` — buffer-info maps\n- `wlift_image` — pixel + metadata maps\n\n\nNo regression test added yet. Recommended next step: write\n`tests/plugin_gc_stress.rs` with `WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1` (forces\nnursery every alloc) — reproduces the corruption in \u003c1s\npre-patch, pins the contract post-patch.\n\n\n20s procedural-world AOT soak — clean (exit 143, SIGTERM only).\n923/923 lib + 21/21 aot_runtime tests pass.\n\n\nUser reported \"segfaults after a while\" with the post-9aeabba binary\nrunning procedural-world. An exhaustive adversarial-verified audit\n(3-vote refute panel) of all 56 `extern \"C\" fn` foreign methods in\nwlift_gpu + wlift_window turned up four additional confirmed\nvulnerable sites — same pattern, same fix:\n\n| File | Function | Risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| wlift_gpu/src/lib.rs:712-752 | wlift_gpu_device_info | map + 3 key strings carried across alloc_string calls |\n| wlift_gpu/src/lib.rs:4103-4205 | wlift_gpu_surface_configure | map carried across 2× alloc_string + map_set |\n| wlift_window/src/lib.rs:460-488 | wlift_window_size | map carried across 2× alloc_string |\n| wlift_window/src/lib.rs:626-749 | wlift_window_handle | map + key_platform across ~30 ops + 7 match arms |\n\n`wlift_window_handle` is the most likely to actually fire — ~30\nallocator calls in series makes nursery-GC interleaving statistically\nnear-certain even though the function only runs once per surface bind.\nThe other three are lower call-rate but still real.\n\nAll four functions had comments CLAIMING they followed the rooting\npattern of `wlift_image_decode`, but none actually invoked\n`roots_snapshot` / `push_root` / `reload_root`. The mistake was in the\nmental model: `set_return(vm, map)` was treated as if it kept the\nRust local valid, but it only roots slot 0 — the Rust local still\nholds pre-promotion bits.\n\nLesson: comments asserting \"this follows the rooting pattern\" are not\nenough — verify the primitives are actually called. A grep-based\ncheck (`rg \"alloc_(string|map|list)\" plugins/.../lib.rs` + audit each\nhit for `push_root`/`reload_root` in same function) catches this.\n\n\nThe adversarial workflow at run wf_6af2ac88-874 enumerates every\nforeign method, audits each against the bug class, and runs a 3-vote\nrefute panel on every vulnerable verdict. Run again whenever a new\nplugin or foreign method ships before declaring \"GC root miss fixed\".","files":null}]}